# Paths stylelint must not lint.
#
# Patterns use gitignore syntax and are anchored to this directory, the package
# root that `npm run lint:styles` runs from.
#
# This list is deliberately minimal, and it is meant to stay that way. Every
# entry here is silently exempt from token indirection (R3) and from flip-safe
# directional authoring (R6), because an ignored file is an unchecked file. Only
# installed dependency trees and generated reports belong here. Authored Blitzy
# code never does.
#
# Do not add:
#
#   * /resources/, /skinStyles/, or any individual stylesheet. Every authored
#     stylesheet stays linted — the token modules, the component stylesheets,
#     the layouts, the core-variable override and all twelve skinStyles
#     overrides. Keeping them in the lint surface is how R3 and R6 are verified.
#
#   * resources/skins.blitzy.tokens/tokens.less. It is the one file allowed to
#     hold colour literals, and that exemption is granted in the `overrides`
#     block of .stylelintrc.json, where a reviewer reading the rule
#     configuration can see it. Listing the file here instead would hide the
#     same exemption behind a second, invisible mechanism.
#
#   * /design/. design/reference/blitzy-tokens.source.less is committed
#     reference material rather than authored code, but it lints clean exactly
#     as its origin wrote it, so it needs no exemption and stays linted.
#
#   * /screenshots/. The captures are PNGs and their audits are JSON; no tool
#     writes a stylesheet there.
#
#   * a stylesheet that fails. When stylelint reports a problem, fix the
#     stylesheet. This file is not an escape hatch from the zero-warning build
#     (Gate 2), and inline suppression directives are prohibited too.

# Installed dependency trees. Neither is committed; both are recreated by
# `npm ci` and `composer install`.
/node_modules/
/vendor/

# Generated coverage reports. These are committed deliverables, but the HTML
# assets inside them are stylesheets shipped by the coverage reporters, not
# code this package authors or controls.
/coverage/
